File Index

/App.css
Purpose: App chrome styling (header, nav tabs, main layout).

/App.test.tsx
Purpose: Smoke test that the shell renders and switches sections.

/App.tsx
Purpose: Top-level tab shell — Areas/Rooms/Mobs/Objects/Resets/Scripts/Socials/Skills/World/Map/Access/Roles/My Content/Engine section nav rendering the matching feature page; holds the areaTarget lift so the World dashboard's cross-area links land on the Areas tab, the roomsTarget lift so a Map room click or the Simulate pane's reverse link lands on the Rooms tab with that room selected, and (Phase 13) the resetsRoomTarget lift so a RoomEditor "see what spawns here" link lands on the Resets tab filtered to that room. Phase 15 adds the Engine tab (EnginePage) — always rendered unconditionally like every other tab; EnginePage itself decides what to show based on capabilities().rebuildEnabled and rebuildStatus().canTrigger, not App.tsx. 2026-07-26 (Areas dashboard redesign): both AreasPage and RoomsPage are full, independent room editors now — a mapFocus lift ({file, vnum}) sends either page's blocked-delete "Go fix it on the Map" button to the Map tab with that room focused/highlighted (MapPage's initialFocus prop); both pages gained the identical onGoToResets (reuses resetsRoomTarget)/onGoToMap/onGoToMobs/onGoToScripts prop shape for their DeleteBlockersPanel's "Go fix it" buttons (mobs/scripts are a plain tab switch — no deep-filter target exists for those two yet). AreasPage's own former onEditRoom hand-off to Rooms was removed — Areas edits directly now, it has nothing to hand off. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): MobsPage/ObjectsPage also gained onGoToResets/onGoToMap/onGoToScripts (each page only accepts the subset that's structurally reachable for its own entity kind — see each page's own .annotated entry for exactly which and why) — all plain setSection(...) switches, none has a vnum-scoped deep-filter target the way Rooms' onGoToResets/onGoToMap do. Phase G: adds the Roles tab (RolesPage) and My Content tab (ContentPage) — RolesPage takes no props (self-contained probe/manage); ContentPage takes an `onLoad(kind, data)` callback that sets a new `contentLoad` lift and switches to the matching tab via SECTION_BY_SNIPPET_KIND, feeding a `pendingSnippet` prop now accepted by RoomsPage/MobsPage/ObjectsPage/ScriptsPage (each seeds a brand-new entity from the snippet's data via the same "+ Add" machinery they already had, discarding the snippet's stored vnum in favor of a freshly-allocated one).

/index.css
Purpose: Global reset + base typography.

/main.tsx
Purpose: Vite/React entry point mounting App. 2026-07-26 (bug fix): forces a real `window.location.reload()` on a `pageshow` event with `e.persisted===true` — the app has no router (every tab/area/map selection is plain in-memory React state), so without this a browser back/forward-cache (bfcache) restore resurrects an OLD cached JS heap/DOM snapshot verbatim instead of the live app, which read to the user as "the Map tab randomly jumps to a previously-selected area" on Back — each Back press could land on a DIFFERENT historical bfcache snapshot, not a single consistent "previous" state, matching the reported symptom exactly.
